# promise: #848
# A Little Window opened by a link from another app shows its page. On the reporter's macOS 27.2.1 it came up
# white and stayed white until the window was resized or the page reloaded: Chromium didn't draw a page left
# hidden, or laid out for another size, as the window arrived. Now Cra looks at the page once the window is up
# (LittlePageHealth): a page in sight that doesn't draw is shown again and resized once, as the reporter's resize
# did. littleBreakNextShow leaves the page as it was found: its view hidden, or laid out at the grow-in's 48 x 30
# start. Needs the screen: only a window nothing covers is judged.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
pace 0.5

# A link as usual: the page draws, and the check says so.
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=plain
expect-log little window page drawing \(came up\): window in sight
cra://debug?littlePage=plain
expect-log little page plain: drawing

# The page left hidden as the window came up: shown again, and drawing.
cra://debug?littleBreakNextShow=hide
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=hidden
expect-log little window page broken for the test: hide
expect-log little window page not drawing \(came up: its view is hidden[^)]*\): shown again
expect-log little window page drawing again
cra://debug?littlePage=hidden
expect-log little page hidden: drawing

# Laid out at the grow-in's start in the full-size window: resized, and drawing at its size.
cra://debug?littleBreakNextShow=size
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=size
expect-log little window page broken for the test: size
expect-log little window page not drawing \(came up: laid out at 48x30 in a [0-9]+x[0-9]+ view\): shown again
expect-log little window page drawing again
cra://debug?littlePage=size
expect-log little page size: drawing
reject-log still not drawing, left alone
